# 2026-11-17 00:53:47.309279
+Role: Expert AI Quant Developer & Trading Systems Architect.
+
+Objective: Build an autonomous, machine-learning-driven scalping engine for Binance USDT pairs targeting highly accurate short-term trades (~95% confidence).
+
+CRITICAL RULE: ABSOLUTELY NO hardcoded threshold rules (e.g., "if RSI < 30 buy"). The system must not rely on simplistic logic. Instead, it must use an ML model (e.g., Random Forest, XGBoost, or a Neural Network) to weigh multiple dynamic inputs and output a probability score.
+
+Core Components to Build:
+1. Data Pipeline: Fetch real-time and historical OHLCV + Order Book data for top volume Binance USDT pairs using CCXT (Public endpoints).
+2. Feature Engineering: Generate a massive feature matrix using `pandas-ta` (indicators), detect historical support/resistance zones dynamically, and implement advanced trading logic inspired by top quantitative "trader skills" GitHub repositories.
+3. Sentiment & News: Ingest real-time crypto news (e.g., CryptoPanic API or RSS) to act as a dynamic risk and volatility filter.
+4. AI Decision Engine: The ML model will ingest the feature matrix and output a precise trading signal.
+5. Signal Output: The final output must be a clean report displaying:
+   - Best Coin to Trade (USDT pair).
+   - Exact Entry Price.
+   - Exact Take Profit & Stop Loss.
+   - Confidence / Probability Percentage.
+
+Execution Plan:
+Task 1: Generate a comprehensive `requirements.txt` file (ccxt, pandas_ta, scikit-learn, xgboost, etc.).
+Task 2: Write `data_pipeline.py` to asynchronously fetch top 20 volume USDT pairs from Binance and their 5m/15m OHLCV data. 
+Please execute these two tasks first, explain your code, and wait for my approval before moving to the ML model.

